From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 22:30:00 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] kicad-cli pcb upgrade: do not crash when the board fails to
 load (backport of the master fix)

getBoard() returns nullptr when loading fails (e.g. a board written by the
Eagle importer with items on an UNDEFINED layer); JobUpgrade dereferenced it.
master already has the same check.

Found by tools/bughunt (pcb import of an Eagle board, then pcb upgrade).
---
--- a/pcbnew/pcbnew_jobs_handler.cpp
+++ b/pcbnew/pcbnew_jobs_handler.cpp
@@ -2691,6 +2691,10 @@
     {
         IO_RELEASER<PCB_IO> pi( PCB_IO_MGR::FindPlugin( PCB_IO_MGR::KICAD_SEXP ) );
         BOARD*              brd = getBoard( job->m_filename );
+
+        if( !brd )
+            return CLI::EXIT_CODES::ERR_INVALID_INPUT_FILE;
+
         if( brd->GetFileFormatVersionAtLoad() < SEXPR_BOARD_FILE_VERSION )
             shouldSave = true;
 
